direction: down

title: |md
  # chrome-tab-remote — proposed architecture
| {near: top-center}

user: User {
  shape: person
}

chrome: Chrome (user's real browser) {
  tab: Granted tab {
    cs: Content script\n(injected on grant only)
  }
  ext: Extension (MV3) {
    style.fill: "#eef6ff"
    panel: Side panel\n(select tab, approve, audit)
    core: Service worker\n(grant store, lifecycle, policy)
  }
}

bridge: Native messaging host\n(local process) {
  style.fill: "#fff7e6"
  mcp: MCP server\n(tools: snapshot, click, fill, ...)
}

agent: Agent backend\n(any MCP client:\nlocal agent, Claude, custom) {
  style.fill: "#f3f0ff"
}

user -> chrome.ext.panel: 1. selects tab,\ngrants access (gesture)
chrome.ext.core -> chrome.tab.cs: 2. inject via\nchrome.scripting (tabId only)
agent -> bridge.mcp: 3. MCP tool call\n(snapshot / act)
bridge.mcp -> chrome.ext.core: 4. relay\n(stdio <-> runtime port)
chrome.ext.core -> chrome.ext.panel: 5. consequential action?\n-> approval gate
chrome.tab.cs -> chrome.ext.core: 6. a11y-tree snapshot,\naction results
chrome.ext.core -> bridge.mcp: 7. result + ack\n(operation lifecycle)
